15 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart titled "Herbal Pharmacopoeia of Ecuador" showing six stages: 1\) Assessment of potential, including biodiversity analysis. 2\) Prioritization and selection, involving criteria establishment. 3\) Development of monographs, with writing and approval. 4\) Establishment of standards, including quality standards. 5\) Implementation and monitoring, with training. 6\) Promotion and dissemination, involving pharmacopoeia dissemination. Each stage has associated tasks.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 28 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
16 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Line graph showing scientific production from 1995 to 2030, with a sharp increase after 2020. The trend line has an R-squared value of 0.7814, indicating a strong correlation.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 29 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Network visualization showing international collaboration. Larger nodes like "China," "India," and "United States" indicate higher collaboration. Connections link countries such as Italy, Germany, and Japan. VOSviewer logo is present.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 29 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/A 42 0 R
/Alt (Network visualization map created with VOSviewer showing clusters of related terms in herbal medicine research. Terms like "medicinal plant," "herbal medicine," "phytoactivity," and "anti-inflammatory activity" are interconnected. Different cluster colors indicate thematic groupings, with lines representing relationships between terms.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 32 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
